SEP-16 (+ mesh twin of GRA-09): meshGeomLoadScot() reads node labels from [baseval, ...) instead of [vnodbas, ...), never stores dimnnbr.
m16u.msh: 2 elements (labels 0,1) then 4 nodes (labels 2..5), base 0; m16u.xyz: coordinates keyed by the node labels 2..5.
  ./geoload m16u.msh m16u.xyz   pristine -> "ERROR: meshGeomLoadScot: vertex geometry data not found (0)" load=1  (element labels were looked up)
                                patched  -> load=0 check=0, dimnnbr=2, coordinates of nodes 0..3 printed, geometry saved back with labels 2..5
(With pristine, the saved geometry of any mesh loaded this way is empty since dimnnbr stays 0.)
Fixed by patches/0008 (and 0011 for the labelled round trip); regression test: test_scotch_mesh_geom with data/small2.{msh,xyz} and small2_lbl.{msh,xyz}.
